{"name":"Stellar Explorer","what":"An explorable 3D map of the night sky: fly between 117k stars, open any into a detail view, with sound tied to the journey.","glance":[["Renders","117k stars at 60 fps"],["Explore","Fly, and expand bodies into detail views"],["Audio","Spatial cues bound to interaction"],["Stack","Three.js + WebAudio in the browser"]],"archHi":"<p>Stellar Explorer is the night sky as one explorable 3D scene: 117,000 stars, and any body opens into its own detail view when you reach it. Moons don't exist until the first time you visit their planet &mdash; each world builds itself on arrival and is torn down when you leave.</p>\n<p>Sound follows the journey.</p>","arch":"<ul>\n<li><strong>One shader program serves every body.</strong> Three procedural surface functions blended by step masks on a type uniform &mdash; no branch in the fragment path, no second program to compile.</li>\n<li><strong>Moons are created on expand and released on collapse.</strong> Geometry, materials and children are walked and disposed, not hidden.</li>\n<li><strong>Five-pass composite.</strong> A tone-mapped render at a capped pixel ratio, then bloom, vignette, chromatic aberration and film grain &mdash; the last three written by hand.</li>\n<li><strong>The background is procedural too.</strong> Three counter-rotating point shells with additive nebula sprites drawn to canvas at runtime; depth and parallax cost no texture assets and no network fetch.</li>\n<li><strong>Hover raycasting at 20&thinsp;Hz.</strong> Hits route by user-data tags, so a single cast distinguishes a click on a body from a click on the void that body becomes.</li>\n</ul>","proc":"<ul>\n<li><strong>No asset pipeline.</strong> One page, Three.js and WebAudio: geometry, nebulae and every sound are generated at runtime. Nothing is downloaded but the code.</li>\n<li><strong>Branchless by design.</strong> The whole sky renders through one uber-shader &mdash; three procedural surfaces blended by step masks on a type uniform &mdash; so there is no program switching and no shader compilation stall mid-flight.</li>\n<li><strong>Resources have an explicit lifecycle.</strong> Worlds are built on first visit and disposed on collapse &mdash; geometry, materials and children walked and released &mdash; so exploration never accumulates memory.</li>\n<li><strong>Interaction feel was tuned before features.</strong> Orbits freeze on hover and in detail view, the camera offsets its target to leave room for the reading panel, and raycasts are throttled to 20&thinsp;Hz.</li>\n</ul>","loCap":"Under the hood — the working architecture.","diagram":"<svg id=\"stellar-light-my-svg\" width=\"100%\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" class=\"statediagram\" style=\"max-width: 560.127px; background-color: transparent;\" viewBox=\"0 0 560.1273193359375 612.5499877929688\" role=\"graphics-document document\" aria-roledescription=\"stateDiagram\"><style>#stellar-light-my-svg{font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Helvetica Neue,sans-serif;font-size:14px;fill:#131311;}@keyframes edge-animation-frame{from{stroke-dashoffset:0;}}@keyframes dash{to{stroke-dashoffset:0;}}#stellar-light-my-svg .edge-animation-slow{stroke-dasharray:9,5!important;stroke-dashoffset:900;animation:dash 50s linear infinite;stroke-linecap:round;}#stellar-light-my-svg .edge-animation-fast{stroke-dasharray:9,5!important;stroke-dashoffset:900;animation:dash 20s linear infinite;stroke-linecap:round;}#stellar-light-my-svg .error-icon{fill:#e7e4dd;}#stellar-light-my-svg .error-text{fill:#181b22;stroke:#181b22;}#stellar-light-my-svg .edge-thickness-normal{stroke-width:1px;}#stellar-light-my-svg .edge-thickness-thick{stroke-width:3.5px;}#stellar-light-my-svg .edge-pattern-solid{stroke-dasharray:0;}#stellar-light-my-svg .edge-thickness-invisible{stroke-width:0;fill:none;}#stellar-light-my-svg .edge-pattern-dashed{stroke-dasharray:3;}#stellar-light-my-svg .edge-pattern-dotted{stroke-das